WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.290
The Teen Titans are starting to grow up.

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:07.020
The first look at the series from San Diego
Comic-Con left many DC fans surprised at how

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.790
bleak the show looks compared to its contemporaries
at The CW.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:14.720
But there's a reason why that trailer was
so dark and gritty, and it has a lot to do

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.800
with the growth of each of the individual
Titan characters.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:23.560
Launching in fall 2018, Titans is the flagship
series of the new streaming platform DC Universe,

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.789
set to bring exclusive DC Comics content to
viewers no matter what device they're on.

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:33.000
It's a major expansion of DC properties on
TV, whether they're animated or live-action,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.980
and Titans is just one part of it.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.640
Titans may not have the sunny disposition
of the CW's Flash, Supergirl, or Legends of

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.770
Tomorrow, and it might be even more angsty
than Arrow.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.310
But that doesn't have to be a bad thing.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:49.250
Taken on its own terms, DC's Titans just might
have what it takes to blow you away.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.620
The jaded Grayson

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.280
The most controversial moment in the Titans
trailer was obviously Robin's F-bomb.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.010
"F--- Batman."

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.449
The apparent shift away from the relatively
carefree Teen Titans tone bothered many, but

00:01:00.449 --> 00:01:03.999
the show's not necessarily as melodramatic
as that trailer moment makes it appear.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.340
"It is very… dark."

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.560
"Of course it's dark.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.350
Night time is the most serious time to fight
crime."

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.970
"Yeah, but I can't see anything, either."

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:18.970
Speaking to Polygon, Titans writer and executive
producer Geoff Johns broke down what exactly

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.549
Robin's angsty issue with Batman might be,
and what it means for the DC Universe show.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:24.549
Johns said,

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:27.970
"The trailer shows a piece of the tone of
the show, the show's not all that.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:31.619
[...] If you look at when Robin first left
Batman in the comics, there was a lot of uneasiness

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:32.920
and him being lost.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.630
Titans is really a series about these different
characters that are all lost in their lives."

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.070
While the phrase may not have hit the right
note with a lot of fans, it does a quick job

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:43.890
of establishing a more complex Robin than
the Boy Wonder many are used to.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:48.390
For casual consumers of pop culture who've
never picked up a comic book, Batman's sidekick

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.680
has often come off as a vexing kid brother
type.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.820
"I want a car!

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.590
Chicks dig the car."

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.750
Titans pushes against this perception, showcasing
a Robin with a chip on his shoulder.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.979
To move out of Batman's shadow, and possibly
become his own hero as Nightwing, he has to

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:11.660
acknowledge that shadow and wrestle with it,
and that's the kind of journey that can only

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:15.580
unfold over a whole season, not just a single
one-liner.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.730
The Outlaw

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:20.310
One of the most promising things we learned
about Titans at Comic-Con didn't show up in

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.870
the trailer, and that's the involvement of
Jason Todd.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:27.340
The second DC comics character to take up
the mantle of Robin, Jason Todd is more popularly

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:31.440
known as the violent hero Red Hood, who stars
in the series Red Hood &amp; The Outlaws.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.709
But long before he two-fisted pistols and
ran with the likes of Bizarro, Todd was a

00:02:35.709 --> 00:02:40.120
loyal ally to Batman, a job which ended when
he was brutally, but temporarily, killed by

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.150
the Joker.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:45.200
Whether you love Jason Todd or hate him, the
character is a linchpin in some of DC's most

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.550
successful comic book stories, including "Death
in the Family", "Under the Hood", and "Hush".

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:54.709
He's also another example of the way in which
Batman hangs over this new series, letting

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:58.970
lower-tier characters fight it out in a world
that's already been defined by more marquee

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:00.200
heroes.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.200
New worlds

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.900
The thing about shared universes is you've
got to be pretty careful about not toppling

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.790
all the dominoes over every time you add a
new piece.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:12.340
Marvel's Cinematic Universe now includes 20
movies and half as many TV shows, restricting

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.180
the kinds of stories that can be told at any
given moment.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:20.810
DC's own Arrowverse is four shows and growing,
with Constantine getting a retroactive inclusion,

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:25.629
Batwoman set to join the universe, and Black
Lightning just waiting in the wings for a

00:03:25.629 --> 00:03:26.629
real crossover.

00:03:26.629 --> 00:03:28.140
It's a lot to keep in mind for any screenwriter.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.650
Titans, on the other hand, is new territory.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.540
As of now, we don't know how Titans will connect
to other DC properties that already exist,

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.239
or if it even will at all.

00:03:36.239 --> 00:03:41.410
With DC Universe rolling out multiple live-action
shows in Doom Patrol, Swamp Thing, and Stargirl,

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:45.341
it seems possible that the streaming service's
shows will be their own shared universe, with

00:03:45.341 --> 00:03:48.060
Titans serving as the start of something new.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.340
"So the theory of the multiverse - that's
true?"

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:50.880
"True.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:51.880
Oh yeah, big time."

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.000
"Yeah, I still can't believe it and I'm from
another planet."

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.390
A clean slate means no baggage, and theoretically,
no restrictions.

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:03.019
The writers of Titans have a rich selection
of DC heroes, villains, stories, and locales

00:04:03.019 --> 00:04:06.879
to choose from, who cares if it accidentally
contradicts something from a show that came

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.269
before?

00:04:08.269 --> 00:04:09.409
Quality source

00:04:09.409 --> 00:04:13.380
While the trailer made Titans look like the
show was betraying the source material, the

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:17.410
truth is that the show's producers are taking
inspiration from the very best in Titans comic

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:18.410
history.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:22.260
Speaking to Polygon, Geoff Johns said the
inspiration for Titans' first season comes

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:27.080
from what he calls "the greatest comic book
Titans run ever": the 1980s New Teen Titans

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.510
stories by Marv Wolfman and George Perez.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:33.470
The influence on the story can be seen in
the trailer, which shows Raven doing whatever

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:37.530
she can to win Robin to her side, just like
in the Wolfman/Perez comics.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:40.880
Raven is the one who brought the team together
to fight her demonic father Trigon.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.660
We don't know for sure if that villain will
appear in the show, but considering the trailer

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:48.970
appears to be all about fighting inner demons,
it wouldn't be surprising if Raven's dad was

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.800
the first season's Big Bad.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:55.471
The Wolfman/Perez New Teen Titans run had
a major influence on DC Comics, and comics

00:04:55.471 --> 00:04:56.471
in general.

00:04:56.471 --> 00:05:01.500
Three DC mainstays in Cyborg, Raven, and Starfire
were all introduced, it was in the pages of

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.220
that series that Dick Grayson went from being
Robin to Nightwing, and it also brought the

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.450
world Slade Wilson, a.k.a. Deathstroke.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.820
Doom Patrol

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:13.790
Joining the Titans on DC Universe are the
team that's been dubbed "the World's Strangest

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.010
Heroes", the superhero squad known as Doom
Patrol.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:21.761
First conceived in the '60s, the title found
a truly unusual voice in the 1980s under writer

00:05:21.761 --> 00:05:25.890
Grant Morrison, who took the reins starting
with the series' 19th issue.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:29.510
Under Morrison's watch, the comic brought
in a truly eclectic group of characters to

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:34.260
root for, from the reality-altering muscle
man Flex Mentallo, to Danny the Street, an

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:36.170
entity of sentient geography.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:40.150
We don't know exactly what version of Doom
Patrol we'll be getting on TV, but we do know

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:43.120
several of its members will be showing up
in Titans first.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:48.320
That series has already cast actors for Elasti-Girl,
Robotman, Negative Man, and the team's leader,

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.160
Dr. Niles "The Chief" Caulder.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.120
In the comics, Beast Boy was an early member
of Doom Patrol, so it's possible he'll be

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.190
used as the connection between the teams.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:06:00.180
There is a chance that some of Titan's stars
might end up on the Doom Patrol show, so you're

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.970
going to want to get in on the ground floor
to see this.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:07.330
As of now, we only know that Titans is premiering
in the fall, with Doom Patrol set to join

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:09.930
the service's programming lineup in 2019.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.860
If you sign up quickly enough, you'll be able
to get 15 months of access for the price of

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.910
one year, which works out to less than $5
a month.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:21.260
We've left a link to the upcoming DC Universe
service in the description of this video.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:25.940
You might even get beta access to the platform,
and get a shot at seeing Titans before anybody

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:27.170
else.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:28.320
Doorways to anywhere

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.060
Speaking to Polygon, Geoff Johns said that
one of the goals with the first Titans season

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:36.000
is to demonstrate that the show can go anywhere,
not just down grim back alleys.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.000
According to Johns,

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.340
"We really wanted to lean into the idea that
every [Titan] is a doorway into another genre.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:45.830
With Rachel [a.k.a. Raven], it's the supernatural
and the horror, and the first season really

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:49.750
focuses on who Raven is and how the Titans
galvanize around her.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.900
You can see that tone in the trailer clearly."

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:56.020
Viewed that way, it makes sense that the Raven-centric
first trailer would have a large amount of

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:00.330
gothic darkness, with the other characters
opening up doorways to different story opportunities.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:05.340
Being an alien, Starfire would seem to offer
a way into science fiction and space opera

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:10.030
stories, while Robin gives us the same world
of noir mystery as his one-time mentor Batman.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.930
As the series progresses and more members
enter the fold, we're likely to be given keys

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.270
to even more worlds and tones of DC.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:20.830
The Titans can solve mysteries in Gotham City,
fight demons in other dimensions, or blast

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.150
off into the stars.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.431
One way or another, the show has a lot more
to offer than just one trailer can show you.

00:07:25.431 --> 00:07:29.320
The DC Universe is just beginning, and Titans
is leading the charge.

